	('battle-battle-of-kolhapur-1659', 'battle-battle-of-kolhapur-1659', 'Battle of Kolhapur', 'battle', 'On 28 December 1659, near Kolhapur, a Maratha force under Shivaji defeated a larger Bijapur army led by Rustam Zaman, who fled the field. It was the Marathas'' second major victory over Bijapur, after Pratapgad. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1659, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-marg-o-1659', 'battle-battle-of-marg-o-1659', 'Battle of Margão', 'battle', 'The Battle of Margão was a military conflict between the Portuguese Empire and the Sultanate of Bijapur that took place in 1659. The battle resulted in a decisive victory for the Portuguese. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1659, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-chakan-1660', 'battle-battle-of-chakan-1660', 'Battle of Chakan', 'battle', 'The Battle of Chakan in 1660 took place between Mughal forces led by Shaista Khan and Maratha forces commanded by Firangoji Narsala at Chakan in Maharashtra. Shaista Khan''s Mughal forces emerged victorious by besieging the Chakan fort, leading to the surrender of the Maratha commander Firangoji. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1660, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-pavan-khind-1660', 'battle-battle-of-pavan-khind-1660', 'Battle of Pavan Khind', 'battle', 'The Battle of Pavan Khind was a rearguard last stand that took place in September 1660, at a mountain pass in the vicinity of Vishalgad between the forces of the Maratha and the pursuing Bijapur Sultanate forces. The recorded point lies within the borders of Bijapur Sultanate that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E61000006FF085C95475524076711B0DE0DD3040', 1660, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-umberkhind-1661', 'battle-battle-of-umberkhind-1661', 'Battle of Umberkhind', 'battle', 'On 3 February 1661, in the Umberkhind pass of the Sahyadri hills near Khopoli, Shivaji''s Maratha forces ambushed a Mughal army led by Kartalab Khan. After about two hours the Mughals surrendered their arms and paid a ransom to be allowed to leave. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E61000006FF085C9544552400000000000C03240', 1661, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-surat-1664', 'battle-battle-of-surat-1664', 'Battle of Surat', 'battle', 'The Battle of Surat, also known as the Sack of Surat, was a land battle that took place on 5 January 1664 and ended on 13 January 1664, near the city of Surat, in present-day Gujarat, India, between Shivaji, leader of the fledgling Maratha State and Inayat Khan, a Mughal commander. The recorded point lies outside the kingdoms mapped in the atlas that year.', '0101000020E61000006FF085C954355240423EE8D9AC2A3540', 1664, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-sinhagad-1670', 'battle-battle-of-sinhagad-1670', 'Battle of Sinhagad', 'battle', 'The Battle of Sinhagad, also known as Battle of Kondhana, involved an attack by Marathas during the night of 4 February 1670 on the Mughal fort of Sinhagad, near the city of Pune, Maharashtra. The Marathas captured the fort. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1670, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-saraighat-1671', 'battle-battle-of-saraighat-1671', 'Battle of Saraighat', 'battle', 'The Battle of Saraighat was a naval battle fought in 1671 between the Mughal Empire, and the Ahom Kingdom on the Brahmaputra river at Saraighat, now in Guwahati, Assam, India. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1671, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-attack-in-hooghly-1671', 'battle-attack-in-hooghly-1671', 'Attack in Hooghly', 'battle', 'The Attack in Hooghly was a Danish attack on two Bengali ships during the Dano-Mughal War in 1671. The Danes succeeded in blowing up the Bengali ships, and violence continued off the coasts of Kalingapatnam and Balasore. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E6100000295C8FC2F51856406666666666E63640', 1671, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-kohat-1674', 'battle-battle-of-kohat-1674', 'Battle of Kohat', 'battle', 'The Battle of Kohat was a military engagement fought in 1674 between the forces of the Bangash tribe and the Afridi tribe of the Pashtun. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1674, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-guler-1696', 'battle-battle-of-guler-1696', 'Battle of Guler', 'battle', 'The Battle of Guler was fought between Mughal forces led by Hussain Khan, and the Raja of Guler, aided by the Akal Sena. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1696, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-anandpur-1700', 'battle-battle-of-anandpur-1700', 'Battle of Anandpur', 'battle', 'The Battle of Anandpur was fought at Anandpur, between the armies of the Sikh Guru Gobind Singh and the Mughal forces aided by the Nawab of Bahawalpur state, Rajas of the Sivalik Hills. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1700, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-satara-1700', 'battle-battle-of-satara-1700', 'Battle of Satara', 'battle', 'The Battle of Satara was fought between the Mughal Empire and Maratha Kingdom between December 1699 and 21 April 1700. The battle started when the Mughal Emperor Aurangzeb personally marched towards Satara, accompanied by 10,000 Mughal soldiers. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E61000001F85EB51B87E5240AE47E17A14AE3140', 1700, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-taragarh-1700', 'battle-battle-of-taragarh-1700', 'Battle of Taragarh', 'battle', 'The Battle of Taragarh was fought between the Sikh forces led by Sahibzada Ajit Singh and the Rajas of the Sivalik Hills. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1700, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-diu-1509', 'battle-battle-of-diu-1509', 'Battle of Diu', 'battle', 'The Battle of Diu was a naval battle fought on 3 February 1509 in the Arabian Sea, in the port of Diu, India, between the Portuguese Empire and a joint fleet of the Sultan of Gujarat, the Mamlûk Burji Sultanate of Egypt and the Zamorin of Calicut. The recorded point lies outside the kingdoms mapped in the atlas that year. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1509, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-chanderi-1528', 'battle-battle-of-chanderi-1528', 'Battle of Chanderi', 'battle', 'The Battle of Chanderi or  Siege of Chanderi took place in the aftermath of the Battle of Khanwa in which the Mughal Emperor Babur had defeated the Rajput Confederacy and firmly establish Mughal rule while crushing regrowing Rajput powers as the battle was fought for supremacy of Northern India between Rajputs and Mughals. The recorded point lies outside the kingdoms mapped in the atlas that year. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1528, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-ghaghra-1529', 'battle-battle-of-ghaghra-1529', 'Battle of Ghaghra', 'battle', 'The Battle of Ghaghra, fought in 1529, was a major battle for the conquest of India by the Mughal Empire. It followed the first Battle of Panipat in 1526 and the Battle of Khanwa in 1527. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria). The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1529, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-salher-1672', 'battle-battle-of-salher-1672', 'Battle of Salher', 'battle', 'In February 1672, near the fort of Salher in Nashik district, Maratha forces under Prataprao Gujar and Moropant Pingle defeated a larger Mughal force. It is described as the first battle in which the Mughals lost in the open field. The recorded point lies outside the kingdoms mapped in the atlas that year. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1672, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-waliyan-1221', 'battle-battle-of-waliyan-1221', 'Battle of Waliyan', 'battle', 'Fought in 1221 during the Mongol invasion of the Khwarazmian Empire at Waliyan, before the Battle of Parwan. The battle location is not recorded here.', '0101000020E610000000917EFB3A385140A1D634EF38BD4140', 1221, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-fatehpur-1519', 'battle-battle-of-fatehpur-1519', 'Battle of Fatehpur', 'battle', 'Fought in 1519 at Fatehpur in Sindh by the forces of Shah Beg Arghun against the Samma dynasty. The battle location is not recorded here.', '0101000020E6100000091B9E5E29FB5040AC8BDB6800BF3840', 1519, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-skirmish-at-pipli-1640', 'battle-skirmish-at-pipli-1640', 'Skirmish at Pipli', 'battle', 'Naval engagement off Pipli in Orissa between the Dutch East India Company and Portuguese vessels.', '0101000020E6100000F697DD9387D55540386744696F903540', 1640, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-mandavgad-1437', 'battle-battle-of-mandavgad-1437', 'Battle of Mandavgad', 'battle', 'Battle fought near Mandavgad (Mandu) in 1437 CE between the Sultanates of Malwa and Mewar. The exact battlefield coordinates are not recorded.', NULL, 1437, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('rajaraja-conquests', 'rajaraja-conquests', 'Rajaraja I''s southern and Sri Lankan campaigns', 'major_event', 'Rajaraja I''s armies conquer the Pandya and Kerala lands and northern Sri Lanka, and in 1004 defeat a Chalukya army in the Gangavadi region of the Deccan.', NULL, 985, 1014, 'about', 'about', 'likely'),
	('gangaikondacholapuram-founding', 'gangaikondacholapuram-founding', 'Founding of Gangaikonda Cholapuram', 'major_event', 'Rajendra I founds a new Chola capital, c. 1025, to celebrate his victory in the north. The name means “the city of the Chola who took the Ganges”.', NULL, 1025, NULL, 'about', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('talikota', 'talikota', 'Battle of Talikota', 'major_event', 'An alliance of five Deccan sultanates defeats Vijayanagara''s army on 23 January 1565. Hampi''s royal centre is plundered and never rebuilt, and the rulers move south to Penukonda. Historians now doubt the older accounts that the whole city was destroyed.', NULL, 1565, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('kailasa-temple-construction', 'kailasa-temple-construction', 'Construction of the Kailasa Temple at Ellora', 'major_event', 'Under Krishna I, the Kailasa Temple at Ellora is cut downward out of a single rock face — one of the largest rock-cut buildings in the world.', NULL, 756, 773, 'about', 'about', 'likely'),
	('chennakeshava-temple-consecration', 'chennakeshava-temple-consecration', 'The Chennakeshava Temple at Belur is dedicated', 'major_event', 'Vishnuvardhana commissions the Chennakeshava Temple at Belur, dedicated to Vishnu, in 1117.', NULL, 1117, NULL, 'about', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('rajaraja-anuradhapura', 'rajaraja-anuradhapura', 'Rajaraja I takes Anuradhapura', 'major_event', 'Chola forces take the old Sri Lankan capital (Wikipedia''s articles give 992 or 993). The Cholas hold the north of the island until Vijayabahu I drives them out in 1070.', NULL, 993, NULL, 'about', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('kannauj-taken', 'kannauj-taken', 'Nagabhata II takes Kannauj', 'major_event', 'The Pratihara king Nagabhata II defeats Chakrayudha and proclaims himself king of Kannauj. The Pratiharas, Palas and Rashtrakutas had been fighting over the throne of Kannauj since 785.', NULL, 816, NULL, 'about', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('delhi-sultanate-founded', 'delhi-sultanate-founded', 'Aibak becomes the first Sultan of Delhi', 'major_event', 'After Muhammad of Ghor is assassinated in 1206, his general Qutb ud-Din Aibak takes power on 25 June and rules independently from Lahore. Formal recognition came in 1208–09. This is counted as the start of the Delhi Sultanate.', NULL, 1206, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('bahmani-founded', 'bahmani-founded', 'Founding of the Bahmani Sultanate', 'major_event', 'Deccan nobles in rebellion crown Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah at Gulbarga (Hasanabad) on 3 August 1347, founding the first independent Muslim sultanate of the Deccan.', NULL, 1347, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-ucha-1222', 'battle-battle-of-ucha-1222', 'Battle of Ucha', 'battle', 'Siege and battle at Uch (Ucha) in 1222 CE during campaigns in the Indus valley. The exact battlefield coordinates are not recorded.', NULL, 1222, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-purandar-1665', 'battle-battle-of-purandar-1665', 'Battle of Purandar', 'battle', 'The Battle of Purandar was fought between the Mughal Empire and the Marathas in 1665. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1665, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-vatapi-642', 'battle-battle-of-vatapi-642', 'Battle of Vatapi', 'battle', 'The Battle of Vatapi was a decisive engagement which took place between the Pallavas and Chalukyas near the Chalukya capital of Vatapi in 642. The battle resulted in the defeat of the Chalukya king Pulakeshin II in 642 CE and the commencement of Pallava occupation of Vatapi lasted until 654. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 642, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-rasil-644', 'battle-battle-of-rasil-644', 'Battle of Rasil', 'battle', 'The Battle of Rasil was fought in 644 CE in present-day Pakistan. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 644, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-chabuheluo-647', 'battle-battle-of-chabuheluo-647', 'Battle of Chabuheluo', 'battle', 'The Battle of Chabuheluo was a battle that took place between an alliance led by the Tang dynasty and the Kingdom of Kannauj in 648 AD. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 647, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-badghis-654', 'battle-battle-of-badghis-654', 'Battle of Badghis', 'battle', 'Battle of Badghis, 654. Wikidata records its date; there is no article that describes this battle on its own. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 654, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-aror-712', 'battle-battle-of-aror-712', 'Battle of Aror', 'battle', 'The Battle of Aror took place in 712 AD between the Umayyad forces under Muhammad ibn al-Qasim and the army of the Brahmin dynasty of Sindh under Raja Dahir. At the Battle of Aror, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim was met by Dahir''s forces in battle. The recorded point lies outside the kingdoms mapped in the atlas that year.', '0101000020E6100000098A1F63EE3E51406666666666A63B40', 712, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-qandabil-720', 'battle-battle-of-qandabil-720', 'Battle of Qandabil', 'battle', 'In 720, the sons of al-Muhallab, who had rebelled against the Umayyads, fled to Qandabil in Sind hoping for refuge. Their ally shut the gates against them, and they were killed fighting their Umayyad pursuer, Hilal ibn Ahwaz al-Tamimi. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 720, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-kharistan-737', 'battle-battle-of-kharistan-737', 'Battle of Kharistan', 'battle', 'The Battle of Kharistan was fought between the forces of the Umayyad Caliphate and the Turkic Türgesh in December 737 near the town of Kharistan in Juzjan, eastern Khurasan. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 737, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-friday-battle-748', 'battle-friday-battle-748', 'Friday Battle', 'battle', 'Armed conflict recorded in 748 CE (Friday Battle). The exact battlefield coordinates are not recorded.', NULL, 748, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-kanchi-803', 'battle-battle-of-kanchi-803', 'Battle of Kanchi', 'battle', 'Battle fought at Kanchi in 803 CE between rival southern dynasties. The exact battlefield coordinates are not recorded.', NULL, 803, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-chach-1009', 'battle-battle-of-chach-1009', 'Battle of Chach', 'battle', 'The Battle of Chach or Battle of Chaach was fought in 1009 AD between the Ghaznavid army of Mahmud of Ghazni and the Hindu Shahi army of Anandapala, near Hazro, resulting in the latter''s defeat. This left the north Indian region vulnerable to further invasions. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1009, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-beas-river-1285', 'battle-battle-of-beas-river-1285', 'Battle of Beas River', 'battle', 'The Battle of Beas River took place between the Chagatai Khanate and the Mamluk Sultanate of Delhi on 9 March 1285. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1285, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-at-machhiwara-1555', 'battle-battle-at-machhiwara-1555', 'Battle at Machhiwara', 'battle', 'The Battle of Machhiwarra was fought between Mughal Empire and Suri Empire in 1555. The recorded point lies within the borders of Sur Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E6100000CDCCCCCCCC0C5340295C8FC2F5E83E40', 1555, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-balkh-1602', 'battle-battle-of-balkh-1602', 'Battle of Balkh', 'battle', 'Campaign and battle at Balkh in 1602 CE. The exact battlefield coordinates are not recorded.', NULL, 1602, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-sangamner-1679', 'battle-battle-of-sangamner-1679', 'Battle of Sangamner', 'battle', 'Fought in December 1679 near Sangamner between the Mughal Empire and Maratha forces led by Shivaji. The exact battlefield coordinates are not recorded.', NULL, 1679, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-gumbat-1675', 'battle-battle-of-gumbat-1675', 'Battle of Gumbat', 'battle', 'The Battle of Gumbat was a military engagement fought in Gumbat between the forces of Khushal Khan Khattak and the Bangash tribe under Sher Muhammad Bangash Kohati. The battle resulted in a defeat for the Khattak forces with Khushal Khan himself being wounded during the engagement. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1675, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-dodah-1680', 'battle-battle-of-dodah-1680', 'Battle of Dodah', 'battle', 'The Battle of Dodah was a military engagement fought in 1680 in the Bangash territory of the northwestern frontier, in the present-day Khyber Pakhtunkhwa region of Pakistan. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1680, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-itakhuli-1682', 'battle-battle-of-itakhuli-1682', 'Battle of Itakhuli', 'battle', 'The Battle of Itakhuli was fought in August 1682 between the Ahom Kingdom and the Mughal Empire in an area that is in modern-day Assam. The Ahoms pushed back Mughal control to the west of the Manas River. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1682, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-kalyan-1682', 'battle-battle-of-kalyan-1682', 'Battle of Kalyan', 'battle', 'The Battle of Kalyan was a series of engagements between the Mughal Empire and the Maratha Kingdom over Kalyan in 1682–83, during the Deccan wars. Mughal forces under Bahadur Khan captured Kalyan on 28 November 1682 after defeating a Maratha force. The battle location is not recorded here.', NULL, 1682, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-bhangani-1688', 'battle-battle-of-bhangani-1688', 'Battle of Bhangani', 'battle', 'The Battle of Bhangani was fought between Guru Gobind Singh''s army and Bhim Chand of Bilaspur on 18 September 1686 or 1688, at Bhangani near Paonta Sahib. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E6100000029A081B9E6E53403E7958A8357D3E40', 1688, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-nadaun-1691', 'battle-battle-of-nadaun-1691', 'Battle of Nadaun', 'battle', 'The Battle of Nadaun, alternatively known as the Hussaini Yudh, was fought at Nadaun, between Raja Bhim Chand of Bilaspur and the Mughals under Alif Khan. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E61000006666666666165340F1F44A5986C83F40', 1691, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely'),
	('battle-battle-of-daman-1694', 'battle-battle-of-daman-1694', 'Battle of Daman', 'battle', 'The Battle of Daman took place on 23 March 1694, when a Portuguese squadron, commanded by General António Machado de Brito, pursued and attacked an Omani squadron sailing off Daman. The recorded point lies within the borders of Mughal Empire that year (per Cliopatria).', '0101000020E61000006666666666365240EC51B81E856B3440', 1694, NULL, 'exact', 'unknown', 'likely');



















































